GNU Unifont 16.0.04, single-width PSF2 face
===========================================

The face ships as src/font_data.rs, a generated module of hex text, not as a
.psf2 file: the target recipe stages module sources through Step::WriteFile,
whose content is a String, so a binary beside them has nothing to carry it and
an include_bytes! of one fails in the target build while every host test still
passes. The hex decodes to exactly the PSF2 whose digest is recorded below.

That PSF2 is not an upstream file. Upstream publishes no
full-coverage PSF2 -- its only PSF is Unifont-APL8x16-16.0.04.psf.gz, which is
PSF1 (magic 0x0436) and covers APL alone. This face is derived from the
upstream .hex release by td-compositor/tools/import-unifont.rs, which pins the
input by hash and is what makes the derivation reproducible.

